## Contribution toolchain

Two CLI tools are required and both are installed:

| Tool | Command | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| drupalorg-cli | `drupalorg` | Issue/MR lifecycle (show, diff, checkout, push) |
| GitLab CLI | `glab` | Pipeline status, inline threads, MR ops |

**`glab` must always be prefixed with `GITLAB_HOST=git.drupalcode.org`** when targeting the Drupal GitLab instance. It is authenticated — no token setup needed.

---

## Issue queue types

Two URL forms are valid inputs to the agent:
- `https://www.drupal.org/project/<name>/issues/<nid>` — classic Drupal.org queue
- `https://git.drupalcode.org/project/<name>/-/work_items/<nid>` — migrated GitLab queue

**Detection:** if `drupalorg issue:show <nid>` returns an empty `<issue_id>` and `<title>`, the project has migrated its issue queue to GitLab. Fetch issue body and comments from GitLab instead:

```bash
# Issue body
GITLAB_HOST=git.drupalcode.org glab issue view <nid> --repo project/<name>

# All comments (chronological, system notes filtered)
python3 .claude/skills/drupal-gitlab-inline-comments/fetch_issue_notes.py project/<name>#<nid>
```

`drupalorg mr:list`, `mr:diff`, `mr:status`, and `mr:logs` **still work** for both migrated and non-migrated projects — only the issue body/comments differ.

